{{!-- A section's title line. Pass `collapse` (the id to remember the fold under)
      to give it a hover fold caret — only where the heading's FOLLOWING SIBLINGS
      are that section's body, which is not true everywhere this partial is used
      (a Lore sub-heading sits inside its own entry box, and the sidebar move
      groups already fold by clicking the heading). Sections that carry an edit
      pencil get their caret from section-edit-toggle instead, so it can sit
      beside the pencil.

      `caret` is the same mark without the button: for a heading that is ITSELF
      the fold control (the Major / Minor arcana sections, where clicking
      anywhere on the line folds it), so the state still reads the same way as
      every other section. Pass one or the other, never both.

      `randomize` is the section key for a "roll one at random" button, sat right
      after the note. Optional like the rest: pass nothing and no button is
      emitted, so every existing caller is untouched.

      `startCollapsed` is forwarded to section-collapse as its `defaultCollapsed` —
      a section that is reference rather than content starts shut. It lives here as
      well as there because a caller needing it had otherwise to bypass this partial
      and hand-write the whole title line, which is how the GM Toolkit's Threats tab
      came to carry four copies of markup this one line emits.

      `headingClass` overrides the heading's own class for the few sections whose CSS
      and whose sheet-side HEADING_SELECTOR key on a different stem. Defaults to the
      move-group title, so every existing caller is untouched.

      WHY THOSE TWO ARE NAMED THE WAY THEY ARE, and the rule for the next one added:
      Handlebars MERGES a partial's hash into the caller's context, so every optional
      parameter here is also a bare lookup against whatever object the caller happens
      to be rendering — `{{#if headingClass}}` cannot tell "the caller passed it" from
      "the caller's own row has a field by that name". This partial is invoked from
      ~45 places, many inside `{{#each}}` loops over view-models built in JS, so a
      parameter named `class` was one VM field away from replacing the heading's stem
      everywhere in that loop. That stem is half of HEADING_SELECTOR
      (StonetopGmToolkitSheet.js) and what the fold walk claims siblings from, so the
      section would stop folding and its caret would swallow the section below, with
      no error and nothing failing. So: an optional parameter here wants a name no
      view-model would use for something else. The remaining ones (`note`, `caret`,
      `randomize`, `searchControl`) fail LOUDLY if they ever collide — a stray note or
      an extra button is visible on the first render — which is why they stand. --}}
<h3 class="{{#if headingClass}}{{headingClass}}{{else}}stonetop-move-group-title{{/if}}">{{title}}{{#if note}} <span class="stonetop-section-note">{{note}}</span>{{/if}}{{#if randomize}} {{> "stonetop.section-randomize" section=randomize title=randomizeTitle}}{{/if}}{{#if searchControl}} {{> "stonetop.tab-search-control" title=searchTitle placeholder=searchPlaceholder}}{{/if}}{{#if collapse}}{{> "stonetop.section-collapse" collapse=collapse defaultCollapsed=startCollapsed}}{{/if}}{{#if caret}}<i class="fas fa-caret-down stonetop-section-caret" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{/if}}</h3>
